171
00:09:50,824 --> 00:09:51,824
Pretty good. What is it?

172
00:09:51,824 --> 00:09:55,824
It's pinne gorgonzola with the meat of a sea king. I really hope you like it.

173
00:09:57,824 --> 00:10:01,824
I've had sea king before, but this tastes different. I like it.

174
00:10:01,824 --> 00:10:04,824
Wow, it really does stretch.

175
00:10:04,824 --> 00:10:06,824
It's soft and squishy like rubber.

176
00:10:06,824 --> 00:10:08,824
Time's up. Step aside.

177
00:10:08,824 --> 00:10:10,824
Come on, just a little longer.

178
00:10:10,824 --> 00:10:11,824
No, bad enough.

179
00:10:11,824 --> 00:10:13,824
This pinnade sea king meat is really good.

180
00:10:13,824 --> 00:10:15,824
Is it hard to eat, though?

181
00:10:15,824 --> 00:10:17,824
What the heck are you doing?! Cut it out!

182
00:10:17,824 --> 00:10:19,824
I can't eat with you pulling my face around!

183
00:10:19,824 --> 00:10:22,824
Sorry, we can't help it. I mean, you're leaving tomorrow, right?

184
00:10:22,824 --> 00:10:25,824
There are a lot of people here who want to touch you just once.

185
00:10:25,824 --> 00:10:26,824
Look!

186
00:10:26,824 --> 00:10:31,824
It's taking forever! I want to touch him now!

187
00:10:31,824 --> 00:10:32,824
Me too! Me too!

188
00:10:32,824 --> 00:10:34,824
Get it? You're really popular!

189
00:10:34,824 --> 00:10:35,824
Hi, Luffy!

190
00:10:35,824 --> 00:10:36,824
I can't wait to touch you!

191
00:10:36,824 --> 00:10:39,824
Dammit! You can't just start a business behind my back!

192
00:10:40,824 --> 00:10:41,824
Come on, Luffy!

193
00:10:41,824 --> 00:10:42,824
Please!

194
00:10:42,824 --> 00:10:45,824
Tonight is the only chance we have to touch a man!

195
00:10:46,824 --> 00:10:50,824
Oh, this is annoying! I can't eat with you pushing me around like this!

196
00:10:50,824 --> 00:10:52,824
I want food not touching!

197
00:10:52,824 --> 00:10:54,824
Wait!

198
00:10:58,824 --> 00:11:00,824
Where did my break go?

199
00:11:00,824 --> 00:11:02,824
Hey, where's the man?

200
00:11:02,824 --> 00:11:03,824
Did he run away?

201
00:11:03,824 --> 00:11:07,824
He couldn't have gotten far. Move out! Let's find him and touch him!

202
00:11:09,824 --> 00:11:12,824
What the heck's the matter with them?

203
00:11:12,824 --> 00:11:13,824
Keep it down.

204
00:11:15,824 --> 00:11:18,824
This was all the food I could grab before I flew out of there.

205
00:11:18,824 --> 00:11:21,824
It's wonderful you'll be with your friends soon. Bet you can't wait.

206
00:11:21,824 --> 00:11:26,824
You said it! Anyway, I'm sorry for all the trouble I started while I was here.

207
00:11:28,824 --> 00:11:30,824
I was real worried when you turned to stone.

208
00:11:39,824 --> 00:11:43,824
But then you protected all of us, didn't you? Back in the arena.

209
00:11:43,824 --> 00:11:45,824
I heard all about it.

210
00:11:46,824 --> 00:11:47,824
You're my hero.

211
00:11:47,824 --> 00:11:48,824
Thanks.

212
00:11:48,824 --> 00:11:49,824
Thanks.

213
00:11:59,824 --> 00:12:01,824
Our dear sister seems troubled.

214
00:12:01,824 --> 00:12:02,824
And she's not eating.

215
00:12:02,824 --> 00:12:05,824
She said she was too tired for the banquet, but she's not going to bed.

216
00:12:05,824 --> 00:12:10,824
Perhaps the forced assembly of the warlords is still weighing heavily on her mind.

217
00:12:16,824 --> 00:12:18,824
Tomorrow morning.

218
00:12:18,824 --> 00:12:20,824
I'm out of my house tonight.

219
00:12:28,824 --> 00:12:30,824
Big Sis!

220
00:12:30,824 --> 00:12:45,184
Granny Mjoln!

221
00:12:45,444 --> 00:12:47,404
Yes, Parker, is something wrong?

222
00:12:48,044 --> 00:12:51,604
No, but the villagers wouldn't stop touching Luffy, so I brought him here.

223
00:12:51,904 --> 00:12:54,784
Ah, well, it's not every day they see a man.

224
00:12:55,404 --> 00:12:56,484
Hey, Granny Bean!

225
00:12:56,824 --> 00:12:59,744
He's welcome to stay here until things die down.

226
00:12:59,744 --> 00:13:01,544
And my name's not Bean!

227
00:13:01,984 --> 00:13:04,204
It seems he has plenty to eat already.

228
00:13:04,444 --> 00:13:05,484
Just bring him some tea.

229
00:13:06,084 --> 00:13:06,604
Okay.

230
00:13:07,644 --> 00:13:10,204
So, Granny, you like reading newspapers?

231
00:13:10,784 --> 00:13:14,844
The cool news isn't delivered anywhere inside of a comm belt, so it's hard to get.

232
00:13:15,064 --> 00:13:19,044
But there are certain perks when your empress is one of the seven warlords.

233
00:13:19,644 --> 00:13:23,184
Even with our isolation, I like knowing what's going on in the world.

234
00:13:24,304 --> 00:13:25,384
Wait a second.

235
00:13:25,764 --> 00:13:26,604
Who's the warlord?

236
00:13:27,444 --> 00:13:28,664
The snake, princess?

237
00:13:29,744 --> 00:13:31,484
Uh, what?

238
00:13:33,764 --> 00:13:39,384
She's one of the warlords, so does that mean she's actually super strong?

239
00:13:39,624 --> 00:13:40,404
You're a pirate.

240
00:13:40,604 --> 00:13:42,664
Surely you know who all the warlords are?

241
00:13:42,984 --> 00:13:43,384
Yeah.

242
00:13:43,804 --> 00:13:44,884
You think so, huh?

243
00:13:45,524 --> 00:13:47,504
Ugh, don't you ever read a newspaper?

244
00:13:48,164 --> 00:13:48,584
Nope.

245
00:13:49,084 --> 00:13:50,044
I sure don't.

246
00:13:51,984 --> 00:13:53,424
Ugh, wow.

247
00:13:53,424 --> 00:14:01,124
The snake princess was crowned ruler of this country, and she was also named the captain of the Kuja Pirates around 11 years ago.

248
00:14:01,524 --> 00:14:09,104
She was still young and inexperienced, but the world government put a bounty of 80 million berries on her head after just one expedition.

249
00:14:09,104 --> 00:14:10,484
What did she do?

250
00:14:10,484 --> 00:14:14,264
The Kuja Pirates were notorious before she became a captain.

251
00:14:14,524 --> 00:14:21,944
Because of that, the world government took an interest in her right from the start, which led to their decision to invite her to become a warlord.

252
00:14:21,944 --> 00:14:25,704
But now her title is about to be revoked.

253
00:14:26,004 --> 00:14:28,904
Since you don't read the papers, perhaps you haven't heard.

254
00:14:32,904 --> 00:14:33,344
What?

255
00:14:34,304 --> 00:14:36,464
The warlords are teaming up with the Marines?

256
00:14:36,644 --> 00:14:38,784
And they're going to have a war with Whitebeard and his crew?

257
00:14:38,784 --> 00:14:39,744
When?

258
00:14:39,904 --> 00:14:40,324
How?

259
00:14:41,644 --> 00:14:43,864
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, hold on a second.

260
00:14:44,324 --> 00:14:47,264
This, this is way too much for me to take in all at once.

261
00:14:50,904 --> 00:14:52,764
What a foolish man you are.

262
00:14:52,764 --> 00:14:54,924
You don't know anything, do you?

263
00:14:56,124 --> 00:14:59,744
Now listen, that was only conjecture at this point.

264
00:14:59,984 --> 00:15:04,244
I don't have any proof, but I'd say that battle is a high probability.

265
00:15:05,364 --> 00:15:08,304
The world government has laid out their bait.

266
00:15:08,784 --> 00:15:12,624
But Captain Whitebeard would never, ever allow his maids to be killed.

267
00:15:12,864 --> 00:15:18,204
But even with that knowledge, they have announced the public execution of Port Custee Ace,

268
00:15:18,204 --> 00:15:21,084
a powerful and high-ranking commander in his crew.

269
00:15:21,084 --> 00:15:44,504
They have announced the public execution of Port Custee Ace, a powerful and high-ranking commander in his crew.

270
00:15:44,504 --> 00:15:46,524
What's wrong?

271
00:15:48,924 --> 00:15:49,484
Who?

272
00:15:49,984 --> 00:15:52,584
Ace, a.k.a. Firefist Ace.

273
00:15:56,584 --> 00:15:58,504
They're gonna execute...

274
00:15:58,504 --> 00:16:10,304
According to this, a pirate named Blackbeard defeated Ace and gave him up to the world government.

275
00:16:10,304 --> 00:16:13,004
In return, they invited him to be a warlord.

276
00:16:17,204 --> 00:16:18,104
Blackbeard, huh?

277
00:16:18,104 --> 00:16:20,504
This sends a strong message.

278
00:16:20,724 --> 00:16:22,844
The government has caught a big fish indeed.

279
00:16:23,144 --> 00:16:27,524
But more than that, if this show of authority can prove that they're stronger than Whitebeard himself, well...

280
00:16:27,524 --> 00:16:28,144
Grinny!

281
00:16:28,304 --> 00:16:28,524
Huh?

282
00:16:30,724 --> 00:16:31,944
He's just my brother!

283
00:16:33,224 --> 00:16:34,944
Port Custee Ace, the Firefist!

284
00:16:35,184 --> 00:16:36,604
You're talking about my brother!

285
00:16:38,604 --> 00:16:38,984
What?

286
00:16:38,984 --> 00:16:43,644
My word! I never knew!

287
00:16:44,004 --> 00:16:46,044
Yeah, and I didn't know anything about this!

288
00:16:46,404 --> 00:16:47,504
He's gonna be killed?

289
00:16:47,764 --> 00:16:49,644
But he can still escape, right?

290
00:16:50,904 --> 00:16:55,804
Well, I'd say that his best chance would be if Whitebeard takes the bait and wins.

291
00:16:55,984 --> 00:16:59,924
Tell me, does it say where they're gonna execute him?

292
00:17:00,584 --> 00:17:05,084
In the town square of Marineford, where Navy Headquarters is located,

293
00:17:05,084 --> 00:17:09,464
it says the execution will take place in one week, that's six days from today.

294
00:17:10,764 --> 00:17:11,784
That's too soon!

295
00:17:12,404 --> 00:17:15,144
How long will it take to get from here back to Sabaody?

296
00:17:15,524 --> 00:17:18,484
Even at top speed, it would take more than a week.

297
00:17:18,724 --> 00:17:19,404
A week?

298
00:17:19,784 --> 00:17:24,864
But that means by the time I meet up with my crew, it'd be too late, Ace would already be dead!

299
00:17:24,924 --> 00:17:25,284
Yes.

300
00:17:25,704 --> 00:17:28,024
Then, how long to get to where Ace is?

301
00:17:28,024 --> 00:17:33,004
Well, if he's being held at Impel Down, that would take, I would say, a week on a pirate ship.

302
00:17:33,004 --> 00:17:35,364
Perhaps four days on a Navy ship.

303
00:17:35,664 --> 00:17:38,564
Whoa, wait! Since when are Navy ships that fast?

304
00:17:38,704 --> 00:17:42,544
There's a sea current that's reserved exclusively for the world government.

305
00:17:43,124 --> 00:17:48,964
From Innie's lobby, to Impel Down, to Navy Headquarters and back.

306
00:17:49,564 --> 00:17:53,504
Think of it as a giant whirlpool that connects those three facilities.

307
00:17:53,504 --> 00:17:59,424
When the Gates of Justice are opened at any of these locales, usually to a Navy vessel,

308
00:17:59,764 --> 00:18:03,724
then the current from the whirlpool changes and ships are ushered inside.

309
00:18:04,344 --> 00:18:09,404
However, if the gates aren't opened, the ship would keep following the natural flow of the whirlpool.

310
00:18:10,504 --> 00:18:14,904
Naturally, most pirate ships would rather skip this current altogether and go the long way,

311
00:18:15,084 --> 00:18:16,644
though it's convenient for the Navy.

312
00:18:17,024 --> 00:18:18,484
Well, what should I do then?

313
00:18:18,484 --> 00:18:24,144
What do you want to do?

314
00:18:25,484 --> 00:18:28,544
Don't tell me. You have your brother's veeber card?

315
00:18:30,504 --> 00:18:34,244
Uh, is that the moving paper that you care so much about?

316
00:18:34,464 --> 00:18:36,244
Nuh-uh. That one was a different one.

317
00:18:36,884 --> 00:18:38,684
This is the card that Ace gave me.

318
00:18:40,444 --> 00:18:43,224
They're also known as the paper of life,

319
00:18:43,224 --> 00:18:46,404
since they give you a hint about the person's state of health,

320
00:18:46,644 --> 00:18:47,964
as well as their direction.

321
00:18:48,284 --> 00:18:50,224
Then, if it's that small, that means...

322
00:18:50,824 --> 00:18:53,904
Back when he first gave it to me, it was ten times bigger.

323
00:18:57,224 --> 00:18:59,804
Looks like Ace has been busy on his own adventure.

324
00:19:03,224 --> 00:19:05,464
There's a little something I wanted you to have.

325
00:19:05,464 --> 00:19:06,544
Here.

326
00:19:09,424 --> 00:19:12,684
Do yourself a favor, and hang on to that.

327
00:19:13,204 --> 00:19:15,244
But it's just to scrap the paper.

328
00:19:15,604 --> 00:19:17,344
That paper will reunite us someday.

329
00:19:17,764 --> 00:19:20,444
I'd tuck it away somewhere, for safekeeping.

330
00:19:21,964 --> 00:19:23,144
You don't want it?

331
00:19:23,864 --> 00:19:25,184
No, I do!

332
00:19:25,184 --> 00:19:27,504
It's perfectly natural for a guy to worry

333
00:19:27,504 --> 00:19:30,864
about his bungling kid brother.

334
00:19:33,204 --> 00:19:36,244
Ace wouldn't be happy about his little brother saving him.

335
00:19:36,724 --> 00:19:38,464
But that's still better than him dying.

336
00:19:41,624 --> 00:19:42,644
Either way,

337
00:19:43,464 --> 00:19:46,004
I'm gonna need to take a little side trip.

338
00:19:46,824 --> 00:19:47,944
Sorry, everyone.

339
00:19:55,184 --> 00:20:06,884
I have to save him.

340
00:20:06,944 --> 00:20:08,424
He's the only brother I've got.

341
00:20:11,924 --> 00:20:13,864
Perhaps you should think this through.

342
00:20:14,524 --> 00:20:17,624
Do you have any idea how reckless this plan is?

343
00:20:17,984 --> 00:20:20,064
You're facing a full-fledged war.

344
00:20:20,704 --> 00:20:23,964
You'll be nothing more than a leaf whipped about by a storm,

345
00:20:23,964 --> 00:20:27,944
an insect flicked away by hands far mightier than your own.

346
00:20:28,164 --> 00:20:29,844
Yeah, that doesn't matter to me.

347
00:20:30,164 --> 00:20:31,444
I still gotta try.

348
00:20:31,764 --> 00:20:34,244
I couldn't live with myself if I let this happen.

349
00:20:34,584 --> 00:20:35,644
I gotta do something.

350
00:20:37,544 --> 00:20:38,884
Yes, I can see that.

351
00:20:40,484 --> 00:20:41,284
So then,

352
00:20:41,844 --> 00:20:44,864
you plan to rescue the most infamous prisoner in the world.

353
00:20:45,644 --> 00:20:48,464
I give you a one in a million chance of success.

354
00:20:48,884 --> 00:20:50,464
But in order to even try,

355
00:20:50,664 --> 00:20:53,384
you need to get to the great prison where he's being held.

356
00:20:53,964 --> 00:20:58,584
Once they transport him to Marinefort,

357
00:20:58,884 --> 00:21:00,804
both the admirals and the warlords

358
00:21:00,804 --> 00:21:03,304
will be keeping a close eye on the situation.

359
00:21:04,124 --> 00:21:04,904
Keep in mind,

360
00:21:05,244 --> 00:21:07,804
because your brother is the most important prisoner

361
00:21:07,804 --> 00:21:09,004
in the Navy's custody,

362
00:21:09,824 --> 00:21:11,524
the prison will be carefully guarded,

363
00:21:11,744 --> 00:21:13,804
and it has quite the fearsome reputation,

364
00:21:14,004 --> 00:21:14,844
if you haven't heard.

365
00:21:15,304 --> 00:21:17,244
It may prove impossible to enter,

366
00:21:17,344 --> 00:21:18,264
no matter what.

367
00:21:18,264 --> 00:21:20,384
I'll worry about that when I get there.

368
00:21:20,564 --> 00:21:21,684
There's no time now.

369
00:21:21,924 --> 00:21:24,404
I gotta make it before they take Ace to be executed.

370
00:21:24,604 --> 00:21:26,064
Give me the biggest ore you've got,

371
00:21:26,184 --> 00:21:27,724
and I'll paddle like hell.

372
00:21:27,844 --> 00:21:29,144
Now, hold on a second.

373
00:21:29,624 --> 00:21:32,124
You'll never reach the prison by determination alone.

374
00:21:32,704 --> 00:21:34,684
There is a slim chance this could work,

375
00:21:34,804 --> 00:21:35,104
but...

376
00:21:35,104 --> 00:21:38,304
the Snake Princess is refusing to follow the order

377
00:21:38,304 --> 00:21:40,104
for the seven warlords to assemble.

378
00:21:40,564 --> 00:21:41,804
But what if that changed?

379
00:21:41,964 --> 00:21:43,544
If she obeyed that order?

380
00:21:43,544 --> 00:21:45,904
We could take advantage of the situation

381
00:21:45,904 --> 00:21:47,764
and sneak you on board their ship.

382
00:21:48,004 --> 00:21:49,264
Wait, what are you...

383
00:21:49,264 --> 00:21:50,904
You mean there's a Navy ship here?

384
00:21:51,444 --> 00:21:51,924
Great!

385
00:21:52,224 --> 00:21:54,164
Then I'm gonna go ask her if she'll do it!

386
00:22:02,884 --> 00:22:04,304
Ren and Ion, it's terrible!

387
00:22:04,884 --> 00:22:05,364
Inishida!

388
00:22:05,624 --> 00:22:06,884
What's all the fuss about?

389
00:22:07,404 --> 00:22:09,064
Thank goodness I found you quickly

390
00:22:09,064 --> 00:22:11,144
when I heard I came as fast as I could.

391
00:22:12,464 --> 00:22:13,284
Heard what?

392
00:22:13,544 --> 00:22:15,064
It's awful!

393
00:22:17,364 --> 00:22:18,804
The Snake Princess!

394
00:22:19,864 --> 00:22:21,624
She's come down with the sickness,

395
00:22:22,304 --> 00:22:24,164
and no one knows what it is!

396
00:22:25,744 --> 00:22:27,164
She's sick!

397
00:22:27,584 --> 00:22:28,184
Oh no!

398
00:22:37,124 --> 00:22:38,764
Please stay strong!

399
00:22:38,764 --> 00:22:50,084
Tell me, am I...

400
00:22:50,084 --> 00:22:54,084
Am I going...

401
00:22:54,084 --> 00:22:58,624
Going to die?

402
00:22:58,624 --> 00:23:09,944
As Luffy prepares to depart Amazon Lily,

403
00:23:10,264 --> 00:23:11,824
Hancock suddenly falls ill.

404
00:23:12,204 --> 00:23:13,624
According to Granny Neon,

405
00:23:13,884 --> 00:23:15,504
Hancock is not the first empress

406
00:23:15,504 --> 00:23:16,584
to fall to this ailment,

407
00:23:16,724 --> 00:23:18,504
and others have lost their lives.

408
00:23:18,884 --> 00:23:20,224
What could have brought it on?

409
00:23:20,524 --> 00:23:21,544
And is there a cure?

410
00:23:21,544 --> 00:23:23,364
On the next One Piece!

411
00:23:23,724 --> 00:23:24,764
Love is a hurricane!

412
00:23:25,324 --> 00:23:26,564
Love, love, Hancock!

413
00:23:26,924 --> 00:23:28,704
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

414
00:23:28,704 --> 00:23:32,604
God bless!

